i2c-i801: the SMBus controllers the prebuilt i2c-i801 knew after Alder Lake-S

Ice Lake-N 0x38a3, Alder Lake-P 0x51a3, Alder Lake-M 0x54a3, Birch Stream
0x5796, Raptor Lake-S 0x7a23, Meteor Lake-P 0x7e22, Meteor Lake PCH-S
0x7f23, Meteor Lake SoC-S 0xae22, with the feature set newer kernels give
them (the Cannon Lake one, as Alder Lake-S has here). Only where i2c-i801
is a module (not on geminilakenk/icelaked, where it is built in).

--- a/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-i801.c
+++ b/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-i801.c
@@ -72,6 +72,14 @@
  * Jasper Lake (SOC)		0x4da3	32	hard	yes	yes	yes
  * Comet Lake-V (PCH)		0xa3a3	32	hard	yes	yes	yes
  * Alder Lake-S (PCH)		0x7aa3	32	hard	yes	yes	yes
+ * Ice Lake-N (SOC)	0x38a3	32	hard	yes	yes	yes
+ * Alder Lake-P (PCH)	0x51a3	32	hard	yes	yes	yes
+ * Alder Lake-M (PCH)	0x54a3	32	hard	yes	yes	yes
+ * Birch Stream (SOC)	0x5796	32	hard	yes	yes	yes
+ * Raptor Lake-S (PCH)	0x7a23	32	hard	yes	yes	yes
+ * Meteor Lake-P (SOC)	0x7e22	32	hard	yes	yes	yes
+ * Meteor Lake PCH-S (PCH)	0x7f23	32	hard	yes	yes	yes
+ * Meteor Lake SoC-S (SOC)	0xae22	32	hard	yes	yes	yes
  *
  * Features supported by this driver:
  * Software PEC				no
@@ -249,6 +257,14 @@
 #define PCI_DEVICE_ID_INTEL_JASPER_LAKE_SMBUS		0x4da3
 #define PCI_DEVICE_ID_INTEL_BROXTON_SMBUS		0x5ad4
